Enforce a JSON Schema on responses with response_format. Type-safe output, no retry on malformed JSON.

OpenRouter ( https://openrouter.ai?utm_medium=email&utm_source=customerio )

Hi there,

*****************************************
Get schema-valid JSON back from the model
*****************************************

Structured Outputs forces a model's response to match a JSON Schema you define. You get type-safe fields back instead of hand-written parsing and retries on malformed output.

Read the structured outputs guide ( https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/features/structured-outputs?utm_campaign=onb-v6-track-b&utm_content=b5-structured-outputs&utm_medium=email&utm_source=customerio )

How it works

Add a response_format with type json_schema and set strict: true:

{

  "messages": [

    { "role": "user", "content": "What's the weather like in London?" }

  ],

  "response_format": {

    "type": "json_schema",

    "json_schema": {

      "name": "weather",

      "strict": true,

      "schema": {

        "type": "object",

        "properties": {

          "location": {

            "type": "string",

            "description": "City or location name"

          },

          "temperature": {

            "type": "number",

            "description": "Temperature in Celsius"

          },

          "conditions": {

            "type": "string",

            "description": "Weather conditions description"

          }

        },

        "required": ["location", "temperature", "conditions"],

        "additionalProperties": false

      }

    }

  }

}

The model returns JSON that matches the schema:

{

  "location": "London",

  "temperature": 18,

  "conditions": "Partly cloudy with light drizzle"

}

Across providers

Structured Outputs works on OpenAI, Google Gemini, and Anthropic models, plus most open-source models. If a model does not support it, the request returns an error instead of guessing. Set require_parameters: true in your provider preferences to route only to providers that support it. For non-streaming requests, Response Healing can repair imperfect JSON before it reaches your app.

To start, add a response_format with strict: true to your next request.

 

→  See models that support it ( https://openrouter.ai/models?order=newest&supported_parameters=structured_outputs&utm_campaign=onb-v6-track-b&utm_content=b5-structured-outputs-models&utm_medium=email&utm_source=customerio )

 

